Chapter: MutBorrowTransitive

 The CL 2710 regression pin. A callee whose RETURN TYPE transitively
 mentions the mutable record only through a record-field chain that
 crosses a List boundary is a borrow - it reads the state without
 handing it on. Recursing into sum/list payloads when walking record
 FIELDS (tried CL 2710) makes this a consume and rejects legitimate
 read-twice code; the field walk must stay sum/list-blind.

Section: Definitions

  mutable ScanState = record {
   pos : Integer
  }

  Trivia = record {
   origin : ScanState
  }

  TokenLike = record {
   kind : Integer,
   trivia : List Trivia
  }

  snapshot : ScanState, Integer -> TokenLike
  snapshot (s) (n) = TokenLike { kind = s.pos + n, trivia = [] }

  scan-twice : ScanState -> Integer
  scan-twice (m) =
   let t1 = snapshot m 1
   in let t2 = snapshot m 2
   in t1.kind + t2.kind + m.pos

  opening : Text = show (scan-twice (ScanState { pos = 7 }))
